    "text": "By Sam DeCoste ,\n5 hours ago WINTHROP (WGME) -- The bumpy road for electric school buses continues for two Maine school districts. Winthrop and Yarmouth are keeping those buses off the road this school year. The Quebec-based manufacturer, Lion Electric, has filed for bankruptcy. Winthrop has four electric buses. Superintendent Becky Foley says the buses have... Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
